Model:       all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (384-dimension sentence embeddings)
Upstream:    https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
             (sentence-transformers, Apache-2.0)
Packaged as: https://huggingface.co/Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2, the ONNX
             conversion of the model above (its config.json records
             "_name_or_path": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2").
             sfgraph downloads it from there with `pnpm models:refresh`
             (scripts/refresh-vendored-model.ts).

Files redistributed (data/Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2/):
  onnx/model_quantized.onnx
  config.json
  tokenizer.json
  tokenizer_config.json
  special_tokens_map.json

Modifications: sfgraph does not modify these files. They are the bytes
published in the Xenova repository, pinned by SHA-256 in data/CHECKSUM.json.
Relative to the original sentence-transformers PyTorch checkpoint, the
Xenova repository's conversion to ONNX and its quantised weights
(model_quantized.onnx) were made by that repository's author, not by sfgraph.
The tokenizer and config files are the BERT tokenizer and model configuration
files shipped with the model.

Lineage (as stated on the upstream model card, not redistributed here):
all-MiniLM-L6-v2 was fine-tuned from nreimers/MiniLM-L6-H384-uncased, which
derives from Microsoft's MiniLM. No files from those base models are included
in this package.

Apache-2.0 licensing of the files above does not extend to the rest of sfgraph,
